hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"21585","Sulayman ibn Dawud and Wahb ibn Jarir said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Jamrah, he said: I heard Iyas ibn Qatadah narrating from Qays ibn 'Ubad, he said: I came to Madinah to meet the Companions of Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and there was no man among them I met more beloved to me than Ubayy. Prayer was established, and 'Umar came out with the Companions of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. So I stood in the first row. A man came, looked in the faces of the people, and knew them except me. So he moved me aside and stood in my place. So I did not comprehend my prayer. When he prayed, he said: O my son, may Allah not grieve you, for I did not do to you what I did out of ignorance. But the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to us: Be in the row next to me. And I looked in the faces of the people and knew them except you. Then he narrated. I never saw men stretch their necks to a thing as they stretched to it. He said: I heard him say: The people of the knot have perished, by the Lord of the Ka'bah. Verily, I do not grieve over them, but I grieve over those of the Muslims who perish. And it was Ubayy. And the hadith is upon the wording of Sulayman ibn Dawud."
"21586","Sulayman ibn Dawud and Wahb ibn Jarir said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Jamrah, he said: I heard Iyas ibn Qatadah narrating from Qays ibn 'Ubad, he said: I came to Madinah to meet the Companions of Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and there was no man among them I met more beloved to me than Ubayy. Prayer was established, and 'Umar came out with the Companions of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. So I stood in the first row. A man came, looked in the faces of the people, and knew them except me. So he moved me aside and stood in my place. So I did not comprehend my prayer. When he prayed, he said: O my son, may Allah not grieve you, for I did not do to you what I did out of ignorance. But the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to us: Be in the row next to me. And I looked in the faces of the people and knew them except you. Then he narrated. I never saw men stretch their necks to a thing as they stretched to it. He said: I heard him say: The people of the knot have perished, by the Lord of the Ka'bah. Verily, I do not grieve over them, but I grieve over those of the Muslims who perish. And it was Ubayy. And the hadith is upon the wording of Sulayman ibn Dawud."
